WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.120
Hi there, welcome.

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.530
This course is all about
initiating a project successfully.

3
00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:10.247
If you haven't gone through
our foundational course yet,

4
00:00:10.247 --> 00:00:12.140
we recommend checking it out.

5
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.777
It covers the foundations of project
management and contains lots of helpful

6
00:00:16.777 --> 00:00:20.642
information for anyone wanting
to start a career in this field.

7
00:00:20.642 --> 00:00:24.250
There are lots of people around the world
like you who are hoping to learn

8
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.440
the skills to get
a project management role.

9
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.149
Maybe you prefer to take
a specialized certification

10
00:00:30.149 --> 00:00:32.619
rather than a four-year degree.

11
00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:37.140
Maybe you're looking for an affordable
way to stand out among competition.

12
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.140
Maybe you are interested
in changing your career.

13
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.940
Whatever your reason for being here,
we're glad you've joined us.

14
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.080
This program is rooted in the belief
that a strong foundation in project

15
00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.160
management can help anyone start
a great career as a project manager.

16
00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:58.040
Before we begin this course,
let me introduce myself.

17
00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:02.026
My name is JuAnne, and
I'll be your instructor for this course.

18
00:01:02.026 --> 00:01:06.213
As a Senior Program Manager at Google for
the past eight years,

19
00:01:06.213 --> 00:01:11.274
I have worked on cross-functional
projects involving product managers,

20
00:01:11.274 --> 00:01:14.766
software engineers,
user experience designers,

21
00:01:14.766 --> 00:01:17.888
network operations, customer support, and

22
00:01:17.888 --> 00:01:23.640
more to build software used at Google and
used by Google Cloud customers.

23
00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.268
I began my career working as a liaison
between customers and engineers,

24
00:01:28.268 --> 00:01:32.246
documenting requirements on
software development projects.

25
00:01:32.246 --> 00:01:34.661
As I became involved in larger projects,

26
00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:39.010
I started to manage the timelines of
the projects and coordinate the work of

27
00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:43.640
the different teams that had to get
involved to finish the project.

28
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.240
Before I knew it,
I was the de facto project manager.

29
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.967
I have accumulated my knowledge
through formal and informal training,

30
00:01:50.967 --> 00:01:55.440
finding practical application in finance,
insurance, and tech companies.

31
00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.888
I'm super excited to be sharing with
you more about the project management

32
00:01:58.888 --> 00:02:00.140
discipline.

33
00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:04.740
During this course, you'll learn all
the steps for kicking off a project.

34
00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.711
We'll start with an overview of
initiation, which is the phase that

35
00:02:08.711 --> 00:02:14.040
allows ideas to come together and form
the beginnings of a plan for a project.

36
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:18.834
You identify the individual components
of initiation like the project scope,

37
00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:21.430
goals, and deliverables.

38
00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:24.700
You'll also learn how to measure
the success of a project.

39
00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.540
This is a super important
piece of the puzzle.

40
00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:32.417
After all, you want to be able to meet or
exceed all of the requirements for

41
00:02:32.417 --> 00:02:34.553
a successful project, right?

42
00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:38.840
Later, we'll talk about how
to identify stakeholders.

43
00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:44.240
Stakeholders have a direct interest in
the project's completion and success.

44
00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.983
We'll teach you about some really helpful
tools you can use to define project roles

45
00:02:48.983 --> 00:02:50.474
and responsibilities and

46
00:02:50.474 --> 00:02:55.840
more tools and resources you typically
need to complete the work of a project.

47
00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:59.721
Finally, we'll introduce documentation
that can help your team prepare for

48
00:02:59.721 --> 00:03:01.040
project kickoff.

49
00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:01.971
Exciting, right?

50
00:03:01.971 --> 00:03:06.840
The skills you learn in this course will
help you start projects of your own.

51
00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.574
We can't wait to get into
these topics with you.

52
00:03:09.574 --> 00:03:10.780
So let's get started.

53
00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:12.360
Meet me in the next video.